{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/98085-when-ordinary-hunters-get-supernatural-powers","id":98085,"title":"When ordinary hunters get supernatural powers...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-24T22:26:36-07:00","id":98085,"title":"When ordinary hunters get supernatural powers...","content":"The higher tier hunters that have supernatural powers have a framework to explain/justify them, and how to deal with things that don't fit their paradigm.<br /> <br /> If a hunter awakens/undergoes the First Change/becomes other splat X, that group will surely get involved.<br /> <br /> But what about the little guys, Tier 1? What happens when hunter Bob finds a nifty bullet-repelling amulet? Or a university student who's stuck with doing all the cell's research realizes he just did a tiny bit of magic when reading from that ancient tome that was handed to him? When the cell is only able to slay the monster with bullets made from an alchemical formula, do they throw away the book when they're done, or do they draw straws to decide who has to build an alchemy lab in their basement, just in case?<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering - sooner or later hunters will come across bits of the bizarre that they can make (somewhat) reliable use of. How do they handle it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T22:32:28-07:00","id":98091,"title":"","content":"That is a broad question, hunters are unique. I mean sure some diehards may go insane at being TAAAINTED with magic, but considering how hunters seem to be able to adapt to conspiracy Endowments its not a super biggy. I mean you could create a Tier 1 Hunter with Psychic powers if your Storyteller allowed it, no real issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:28:06-07:00","id":98191,"title":"","content":"I imagine the opportunity to get some minor magic is actually pretty common in any long term successful Hunter cell; what really sets Tier 3 apart is that they can do it reliably while at the lower tiers, if one guy gets magic then that dosen't help the others get magic - you can learn a spell or find an amulet, but you can't teach the spell or make an amulet. Witchfinders really dropped the ball when it talked about how nearly all hunters fanatically hate witches rather than discussing these interesting possibilities.<br /> <br /> Here's the breakdown.<br /> <br /> Tier 1: It varies, but the more obviously inhuman your enemies are the more likely you are to be comfortable with using a magic trick; that said even a witch hunter or a psychic hunter will find it easy to draw a line if there's something obviously evil about their enemy that can separate themselves from the bad guy (&quot;you see, his magic involves cutting out people's hearts and feeding them to the devil. My magic involves chanting in Hindi while burning intense&quot;)<ul><li>Ashwood Abbey: All for it.</li> <li>Barrett Commission: Probably pro themselves using magic, they might be a little less happy with other members of the compact doing the same.</li> <li>Bear Lodge: Probably ok with it, since they don't really think monsters (werewolves) are evil. Just a worthy challenge to hunt. (You know, I always imagined that a successful Bear Lodge Hunter might get a letter from a different pack saying &quot;congratulations, you are a true hunter and I am honoured to name you &lt;First Tongue word&gt;. Now if you want a real challenge, I live in this forest!&quot;)</li> <li>Division Six: Hell no</li> <li>Illuminated Brotherhood: Well they're trying to enhance their psychic spirit powers.</li> <li>Keepers of the Source: Founded by a psychic, though they'd hate anything that used source.</li> <li>Long Night: Only if they could justifiably call it Christian, and they might think it belongs in a cathedral rather than risked on the battlefield.</li> <li>Loyalists of Thule: Known to have magic, vary careful about using it.</li> <li>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: See that picture <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I personally like to think that they know and are proud of having some witches on the council, but almost no would be apprentices ever cast a successful spell.</li> <li>Network Zero: You got powers? Cool! Pose for the camera. (putting big targets pointed at you on YouTube, bad idea)</li> <li>Night Watch: See Tier 1.</li> <li>Null Mysteriis: This is a good day for science, lets find a lab and test this!</li> <li>Promethean Brotherhood: Guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Talbot Group: Probably trying to get hold of native American spirit magic.</li> <li>Union, The: See Tier 1</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}